# Cloudflare Pages header rules (copied to the build root by adapter-static).
#
# Content-hashed chunks look like the perfect candidates for `immutable`, and
# on a host that answers a miss with 404 they are. This project is served as
# plain static assets, so a hashed file that is not there yet — the seconds
# around a deploy going live — comes back as the fallback page instead. Cache
# that under a .js URL and every later load of the site replays 60 kB of HTML
# where a module should be, until the entry expires. Revalidating costs one
# conditional request per chunk against the edge, answered with a 304, and it
# makes a bad entry heal on the very next load.
/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
